          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy a propane powered generator because propane keeps for years and gasoline does not. For most homes, the Westinghouse iGen5000DFc is the right size, with 3,500 running watts on propane and remote start. For whole-panel backup through a transfer switch, the WGen9500DF's 8,500 propane running watts and 50 amp outlet are the answer. For light loads and camping, the iGen2550DFc is the small propane generator to beat.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, size it on the propane rating, plan your cylinders before the storm, and use a bigger tank in winter. True propane-only portables have nearly disappeared, so treat a dual fuel unit as a propane generator with a gasoline backup, which in a long cold outage is exactly what you want.
